\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 true] [17592186068464 1071 "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle,$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 true] [17592186068464 1071 "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle$," 13194139533385 17592186045585 false] [17592186068464 1074 "Evaluating the function at $t=4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr(4) &= ⟨2 - 4, 2\\sqrt{4}, 4 - 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 4, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid r(4) \\mid &= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + (4)^{2} + (3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4 + 16 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 false] [17592186068464 1074 "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨2-4,\\,2\\sqrt{4},\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 true] [17592186068465 1071 "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi$." 13194139533385 17592186045585 false] [17592186068465 1071 "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi.$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 true] [17592186068465 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(π) &= ⟨\\cos π, \\sin π, π⟩ = ⟨ - 1, 0, π⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle$.\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\