) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} \\cdot (1 - 0) \\cdot (1 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 false] [17592186105463 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f\\left(x,y,g(x,y)\\right) \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x} = \\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(1+x+y^2\\right) = 1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(1+x+y^2\\right) = 2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be evaluated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z-x+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(1+x+{y}^{2})-x+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{1}^{2}+(2y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+2{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+2{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2(1+2{y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+2{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+2{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\sqrt{1+2{y}^{2}}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\cancel{\\sqrt{1+2{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 true] [17592186105464 1071 "![](images/d8/d8675cb0c59ba915cefe4b0bbe539f1e7e38b5a3ac2fae4bd2bb25e4de96e116.png)\n\nEvaluate the surface integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iint\\