erentiable at\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a\n$$\n\nThen, the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $\\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) \\mid \\approx f(a) + f^{′}(a)(x - a) + \\frac{1}{2}(x - a)^{T}f^{″}(a)(x - a)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂x_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the following data:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(a) &= -1, \\mid f^{′}(a)|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\mid f^{″}(a)|= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the polynomial at $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf(1, 1, 1) \\mid \\approx - 1 + \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}; =-1 + \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}; =-1 + 1 + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}; = \\frac{1}{2}(3); = \\frac{3}{2}\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 false] [17592186198084 107