d}\n$$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 true] [17592186203726 1074 "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n$(a ± b) \\cdot c|= a \\cdot c ± b \\cdot c; c \\cdot (a ± b)|= c \\cdot a ± c \\cdot b$\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n$(λa) \\cdot b|= λ(a \\cdot b); a \\cdot (λb)|= λ(a \\cdot b)$\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n$\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{0}$.\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n$a \\cdot b|=-b \\cdot a$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n$2\\mathbf{a} \\times (\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b})=(2\\mathbf{a}) \\times (\\mathbf{a}) + (2\\mathbf{a}) \\times (3\\mathbf{b})$\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n$(2a) \\cdot (a) + (2a) \\cdot (3b)|= 2(a \\cdot a) + (2 \\cdot 3)(a \\cdot b); = 2(a \\cdot a) + 6(a \\cdot b)$\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{0}{:}$\n$2(a \\cdot a) + 6(a \\cdot b)|= 2(0) + 6(-b \\cdot a); =-6(b \\cdot a)$\n- Finally, we substitute the given value for $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a}$ and simplify:\n$-6(b \\cdot a)|=-6(i - j - 2k); =-6i + 6j + 12k$" 13194139533385 17592186045585 false]] :edb/tempids {"e-10002" 17592186063918 "e-10003" 17592186063919 "e-10008" 17592186068435 "e-10009" 17592186068436 "e-10013" 17592186068437 "e-10014" 17592186183920 "e-10025" 17592186183924 "e-10033" 17592186187992 "e-10034" 17592186091930 "e-10044" 17592186161674 "e-10052" 17592186110293 "e-10053" 17592186110294 "e-10071" 17592186128839 "e-10073" 17592186128840 "e-1038" 17592186096374 "e-1039" 17592186096375 "e-10521" 17592186128841 "e-10535" 17592186183927 "e-10536" 17592186183928 "e-10537" 17592186183929 "e-10551" 17592186192433 "e-10552" 17592186192434 "e-10553" 17592186192435 "e-10554" 17592186192436 "e-1056" 17592186110296 "e-106